1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,500
What could help your shop finish the same order sooner?

2
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:07,000
Explore layout changes, equipment, and material delivery with WorkCell Twin.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Start in the English setup screen and choose an industry template.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:17,000
CNC, food packaging, medical devices, and electronics provide editable starting conditions.

5
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:22,000
Drag a material rack or workbench to adjust the layout.

6
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:27,000
Use Reset Layout to return to the selected industry template.

7
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:31,000
Enter order quantities and the time required at each process step.

8
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Here, Product A changes to six units, with a ten-second inspection step.

9
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:39,000
The comparison recalculates as the input values change.

10
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:43,000
Select a product-change setup time and a rework setting.

11
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:47,000
These are simulation assumptions that can be adjusted for each experiment.

12
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:51,000
Open Compare Options to view four changes under the same order conditions.

13
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Compare completion times first, then inspect the modeled output and cost estimates.

14
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:59,000
The numbers shown here are example simulation results.

15
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:03,000
Switch from the normal order to an urgent mix with more Product B.

16
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:07,000
The four scenario results update together for the new workload.

17
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:11,333
Play the two-dimensional replay to follow workers and material flow.

18
00:01:11,333 --> 00:01:15,667
Positions, queues, and completion counts come from the calculated simulation timeline.

19
00:01:15,667 --> 00:01:20,000
Pause, restart, or scrub the timeline to inspect a specific moment.

20
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:24,000
Select a Watch Moment card to jump to a highlighted point in the run.

21
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:28,000
Inspect the shared equipment and the workers waiting around it.

22
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:33,000
Switch to the isometric view to inspect the layout and worker movement.

23
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:38,000
The camera control changes your view of the same simulated run.

24
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:42,000
Compare All 4 places every scenario in a shared replay view.

25
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:46,000
Look for differences in movement, queues, and completion progress.

26
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Compare the standard FIFO policy with the adaptive scheduling option.

27
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:54,000
In this prototype, adaptive decisions use coded rules, not live language-model agents.

28
00:01:54,000 --> 00:02:00,000
Start with your own inputs and explore your next shop-floor experiment.
